Cell["\<\
This shows that for a small coupling constant (g) perturbation theory gives \
values close to the exact integral. However as g grows the perturbative \
approximation becomes worse, as the underlying series is asymptotic. The \
series is asymptotic as the number of Wick contractions in the term grows as \
a factorial of n (see pdf notes):
(2n-1)!! 

Next...
I will tackle the 1D case, Quantum Mechanics.
This will involve a different approach to the solution whereby we will set up \
a Hamiltonian containing the interaction term, and compute its eigenvalues.
\
